BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhushtripliveinconcert40rockwellbrewery1010268pm26083-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261010T155031Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:HUSH TRIP Live in Concert @ Rockwell Brewery 10/10/26 8PM!
DESCRIPTION:Hush Trip is coming back to THE ROCK for a night jam packed with some of the most iconic and hard driving songs of the past 4 decades. If you've never seen these guys\, Hush Trip is a five-piece rock band delivering a wide-ranging set of popular covers with a deep respect for the authentic sound and spirit of the originals. Their crowd-favorite selections pay tribute to artists like Foo Fighters\, Van Halen\, AC/DC\, Green Day\, Blur\, Lit\, Blink-182\, Audioslave\, ZZ Top\, R.E.M.\, U2\, Incubus\, and many more. With tight musicianship and well-crafted set-lists\, Hush Trip delivers a polished\, memorable\, and engaging show that connects with audiences of all ages. Get ready to enjoy the songs you know by heart and the ones you forgot you loved. Hush Trip is David Truitt (Lead Vocals / Keyboard)\, Steve Davis (Guitar / Engineer)\, Rob Shenk (Guitar)\, Matt McNiesh (Bass / Vocals) & Adam Mason (Drums). Grab all of your favorite friends\, spread the word and don't miss the fun!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/hush-trip-live-in-concert-%40-rockwell-brewery-10-10-26-8pm!/26083/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhauntedhistoryatthenationalmuseumofcivilwarmedicine15484-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261010T155031Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:Haunted History at The National Museum of Civil War Medicine
DESCRIPTION:Starting on October 10th\, tour the most haunted building in Frederick – the National Museum of Civil War Medicine. Explore the building’s history amidst the darkened galleries and offices. On the tour\, staff and volunteers will share stories of Civil War embalmers\, the building’s most infamous tenants\, and their first-hand accounts of paranormal activity that have given the building its spooky reputation. In addition to a trip through the museum galleries\, the tour provides exclusive access to the third floor where numerous sightings have occurred. 48 East Patrick Street was built in the 1830s. Before it became the National Museum of Civil War Medicine\, the building was a furniture shop and a site of Civil War embalming\, as well as home to many Frederick residents and their businesses. The past still echoes through the halls of the building. The haunting sights\, sounds\, and sensations from the building have been reported for decades by the people who lived and worked in the building over many years. Join us to hear our staff and volunteers’ stories first-hand. You are invited to bring your own cameras and ghost-finding apps – who knows what you’ll capture! Flash photography and LIVE streaming are prohibited. Tours will be given on October 10\, 17\, 24\, and 25\, from 5:30 p.m.-6:30 p.m. This year we are offering two special Halloween tours on Saturday\, October 31\, from 5:30 p.m.-8:00 p.m. and 8:00 p.m.-10:30 p.m. During these special Halloween night tours\, you’ll have additional time to tour the galleries without a guide.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/haunted-history-at-the-national-museum-of-civil-war-medicine/15484/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhealthhive26179-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261010T155031Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Health Hive
DESCRIPTION:The Health Hive is a collective space for all things health and wellness\, focused on promoting Frederick/MD local small businesses. Here\, we come together to collaborate with people across all facets of human health. From wellness practitioners\, exercise studios and whole foods\, to regenerative farmers and conscious product and service based companies\, the Health Hive is a place for the community to support each other\, learn\, grow\, and gain access to wellness resources they may not have known was available in Frederick. WellNest is a woman-owned and operated holistic women’s health practice\, with a focus on bio-individuality\, functional nutrition\, cycle syncing\, and fertility coaching. Co-host FITCI is a woman-led 501(c)(3) nonprofit\, and has been Maryland’s #1 business incubator for 3 consecutive years\, helping startup companies grow\, scale\, and thrive. Together\, we are aiming to connect the businesses dedicated to improving the wellness of our community\, to the community itself. The 3rd annual Health Hive is a FREE admission\, family friendly\, fun event to shop\, learn\, and support local. There will be music\, coffee\, juice\, raffle prizes\, and more to enjoy!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/health-hive/26179/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventinsidethefarmsofmonocacy24722-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261010T155031Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Inside the Farms of Monocacy
DESCRIPTION:The Best and Worthington farms are an integral part of the history of both the Civil War and the Battle of Monocacy. Join rangers and volunteers to learn about the people who lived\, worked\, and fought on the farms. Visitors will also get a rare opportunity to tour the first floor of these historic structures. Guest should meet at Best Farm\, tour stop #1 on Monocacy National Battlefield at 9am on October 10\, 2026. Following the tour of Best Farm and its grounds\, guests will be asked to meet at Worthington Farm\, tour stop #2\, by 11am for a tour of Worthington Farm. Space is limited at both farms so please contact Monocacy National Battlefield via their email\, mono_mail@nps.gov or by calling 301-662-3515 to make your reservation.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/inside-the-farms-of-monocacy/24722/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjumbospumpkinpatchfallfestival11483-20261010@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261010T155031Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
SUMMARY:Jumbo's Pumpkin Patch Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season with a full day of festive fun for all ages at Jumbo’s Pumpkin Patch! From classic farm adventures to fall-themed attractions\, our Fall Fun Festival is the perfect weekend outing for families\, friends\, and pumpkin lovers. What’s Included with Admission: Your ticket includes unlimited access to a variety of seasonal attractions: Hayrides through the farm 30+ acre u-pick pumpkin patch (pumpkins sold by the pound) Corn maze (14 acres) Petting zoo Jumping pillow Giant slides Mini mazes for younger guests Playgrounds and yard games General Store with fall shopping and décor​ Optional Add-Ons: (Available for Purchase Onsite - Saturday and Sunday Only) Enhance your day with these fun extras: Pony Rides – $7 Face Painting – $4 Sandy Candy (Edible Sand Art) – $4 Corn Cannon – $5 (3 shots) ​ Food & Drinks: Come hungry! A variety of food\, snacks\, and beverages are available for purchase\, including selections from Liquidity Ale Works of Mt. Airy. Tickets available online or at the gate.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jumbos-pumpkin-patch-fall-festival/11483/
END:VEVENT
